# The build context of tools/basemodel/Dockerfile is the repository root. Only the
# files that the Dockerfile copies go in: the server and trainer scripts, the
# manifest, the pinned requirements, the license and notice, and the synthetic
# bench cases. No vault, no owner data, no Rust tree. The fine-tuned checkpoint
# comes from the named build context `model`, not from this context.
*
!LICENSE
!tools/basemodel/requirements.txt
!tools/basemodel/manifest.json
!tools/basemodel/NOTICE
!tools/basemodel/docker-entrypoint.sh
!tools/basemodel/common.py
!tools/basemodel/app.py
!tools/basemodel/heads_cache.py
!tools/basemodel/serve.py
!tools/basemodel/train.py
!tools/basemodel/bench.py
!tools/basemodel/fetch_weights.py
!tools/finetune/local_train.py
!tests/fixtures/bouncer/cases.tsv
